    "GENERATED by scripts/sync_npd_oos.py from the 'Summary Launch Dashboard'",
    "tab of the NPD OOS Tracking sheet (Demand Planning). Do not hand-edit.",
    "",
    "Real Inventory is refreshed by Demand Planning every Monday, so between",
    "Mondays it is a stock count that is up to a week old and does not move as",
    "units sell. Decay Curve OOS is recalculated more often. Both are shown on",
    "the hub summary ALONGSIDE the Snowflake-derived inventory, never instead",
    "of it: Snowflake moves daily but Demand Planning says it is not always",
    "right, so the dashboard labels both and lets a human decide.",
    "",
    "  decayCurveOOS       Projected out-of-stock date from the decay curve.",
    "  realInventoryUnits  On-hand units per Demand Planning, as of Monday."
